        {"after": "Fungi: eukaryotic, heterotrophic (absorptive nutrition)",
         "md": "**Deep dive — the absorber's lifestyle.** Fungi cannot ingest; they digest outside their bodies. Hyphae secrete enzymes into the substrate, break large molecules down, and reabsorb the small ones. Combined with chitin cell walls (not cellulose) and a stored carbohydrate of glycogen, this makes the fungus a nutritionally unique kingdom: neither plant (no photosynthesis) nor animal (no ingestion), but the world's premier decomposer and recycling agent."},
