        {"after": "## 4. Economic Importance of Fungi — The Full Ledger",
         "md": "**Deep dive — the mycelium is the organism.** A common exam trap: students call the mushroom 'the fungus'. In fact the mushroom is a temporary spore-producing structure; the permanent organism is the mycelium running through soil or wood. The basidiocarp's job is purely reproductive: pack basidiospores onto gills with maximum surface area and let wind or rain-dispersal do the rest. That is why a fairy ring of mushrooms marks the growing edge of one vast hidden mycelium."},
